# Licensing — workspace-program (J-lens representational & causal studies)

This repository is **dual-licensed**. Two licenses apply, depending on whether a
file is *software* or *authored content / data*.

| Scope | License | Full text |
|---|---|---|
| **Software** — source code | **MIT** | below, in this file |
| **Materials, data, preregistrations & manuscript** | **CC-BY-4.0** | [`LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.txt`](LICENSE-CC-BY-4.0.txt) |

## What each license covers

**MIT (software).** Every `.py` file in the repository: the analysis, run, and
verification scripts under `phase0/scripts/`, `phase1/scripts/`, `phase2/scripts/`,
`phase2b/scripts/`, and `paper/` (e.g. `build_numbers_manifest.py`,
`cold_verify_behavioral.py`, `make_figures.py`).

**CC-BY-4.0 (materials, data & documentation).** Everything that is authored
content or generated data rather than executable code:

- **Manuscript & paper artifacts:** `paper/preprint_held_but_not_heeded_v2.md`,
  `paper/references*.md`, `paper/NUMBERS.{md,json}`, `paper/figures/*` (PDF/PNG/CSV),
  and the verification/mentions notes under `paper/`.
- **Preregistrations & provenance:** `PREREG_PHASE1.md`, `PREREG_PHASE2.md`,
  `PREREG_PHASE2B.md`, `PROVENANCE.md`, `phase1_token_sets_SEALED.md`, and the
  phase reports (`RESULTS_PHASE1.md`, `phase2/*.md`, `phase2b/*.md`, `phase0/reports/*`).
- **Materials & datasets:** `phase1/materials_canonical/**` and all generated data
  and logs (`*.json`, `*.jsonl`, `*.csv`, `*.log`) across `phase0/`, `phase1/`,
  `phase2/`, `phase2b/`.

Rule of thumb for a mixed directory: `.py` → MIT, everything else → CC-BY-4.0.

Under **CC-BY-4.0**, reuse requires attribution: cite the work (see
[`CITATION.cff`](CITATION.cff)) and indicate whether you made changes.

## Third-party and cross-repository material (not licensed here)

- **`jacobian-lens`** (the pre-fitted verbalizable-workspace lens and its library)
  is vendored under `vendor/` — **gitignored, not distributed in this repository** —
  and is governed by its own upstream **Apache-2.0** license
  (`github.com/anthropics/jacobian-lens`, commit `581d398…`; see `PROVENANCE.md`).
- **`phase1/materials_canonical/**`** are copied byte-for-byte from the sibling
  **reification-gradient** repository (Study 1 materials, same author, also CC-BY-4.0
  there). They are pinned `-text` in `.gitattributes` so their sealed sha256 stay
  byte-identical across platforms; do not renormalize them.

> **Research-ethics note (not a license term).** The fabricated category "narrative
> dysprosexia" and all synthetic disorder content exist for controlled in-silico
> measurement only. These licenses permit reuse of the files; they do **not** endorse
> presenting any fabricated category as a real clinical entity.

